{"name":"Warmth","hex":"#9f552d","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"warmth","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A moderate degree of heat; the sensation of being warm.","Friendliness, kindness or affection."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/warmth"}],"entries":[{"title":"Temperature","blocks":[{"text":"In classical thermodynamics and kinetic theory, temperature reflects the average kinetic energy of the particles in a system, providing a quantitative measure of how energy is distributed among microscopic degrees of freedom."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/23/Thermally_Agitated_Molecule.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Temperature"},{"title":"Warmth (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Warmth is the third studio album by New York City-based electronic music group Blondes, released on R&S Records on August 11, 2017; they originally released records via RVNG Intl., but as the label moved their business model from issuing dance music to experimental music and re-releases of underground records, the duo moved to R&S to continue producing dance music."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/26/Warmth_%28album%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Warmth_(album)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Thermally_Agitated_Molecule.gif/250px-Thermally_Agitated_Molecule.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/23/Thermally_Agitated_Molecule.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Thermally_Agitated_Molecule.gif/250px-Thermally_Agitated_Molecule.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parse